---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<section class="sec" id="how" aria-labelledby="t-how">
  <h2 id="t-how"><span class="n">4</span> How a claim is checked</h2>
  <p class="lede"><span class="nt">No model in the loop.</span> DocKeeper compares fingerprints of normalized code, so it gives the same answer every time it runs, on your machine or in CI.</p>
  <aside class="mn"><b>The code behind this section</b><code>markdown.py</code> reads the anchors, <code>bloques.py</code> finds the block, <code>huellas.py</code> fingerprints it and <code>motor.py</code> gives the verdict.</aside>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Anchor every claim</h3>
      <p>Next to each sentence, the agent points at the code that proves it: by symbol, by line, hidden in a comment, inside a diagram or stored outside the text.</p>
      <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/markdown.py#analizar -->
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>It becomes a block</h3>
      <p>The whole function, class or method around the anchor, not a fragile line range. Outside any definition, a small window around the line.</p>
      <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/bloques.py#bloque_en -->
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Seal a fingerprint</h3>
      <p>The block is normalized and hashed, so reformatting is harmless and logic changes are not. The seal file keeps hashes and positions, never code.</p>
      <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/huellas.py#normalizar_linea dockeeper/sello.py#Entrada -->
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Check, any time</h3>
      <p>Locally, after every commit or on every pull request. The exit code tells CI whether your docs are still true.</p>
      <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/motor.py#verificar_codigo -->
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="verdicts">
    <div><b class="v-OK">OK</b><span>exit 0</span><p>Same block, same place.</p></div>
    <div><b class="v-MOVED">MOVED</b><span>exit 0</span><p>Same block somewhere else. <code>fix</code> follows it without anyone reviewing.</p></div>
    <div><b class="v-CHANGED">CHANGED</b><span>exit 1</span><p>The code changed. A person reads it and updates the sentence.</p></div>
  </div>
  <figure class="wide">
    <div class="figure-scroll"><img src={`${base}assets/how-it-works.svg`} alt="Diagram: a claim in docs/payments.md is anchored to the whole validate_payment function, the block is normalized and hashed into the seal file, and check reports OK, MOVED or CHANGED" width="960" height="330" loading="lazy"></div>
    <figcaption class="cap">The same example end to end. <code>fix</code> only ever touches the seal file; it never rewrites your documents.</figcaption>
    <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/motor.py#arreglar -->
  </figure>
</section>
